        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c050692d-b8c9-5399-9267-9521a3053bef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Erodium, Cymbidium, California macrophylla, Cymbidium suave\n- Families: Geraniaceae, Orchidaceae\n- Places: North Africa, Indomalaya, the Middle East, Australia\n\nFacts:\n- Erodium is a genus of flowering plants in the family Geraniaceae.\n- Erodium includes about 60 species native to North Africa, Indomalaya, the Middle East, and Australia.\n- Cymbidium is a genus of 52 evergreen species in the orchid family Orchidaceae and is also called the boat orchid.\n- In 1810, Cymbidium suave was described by R. Brown as an Australian orchid species in the genus Cymbidium.\n- California macrophylla was formerly placed in the genus Erodium and was later moved to its own monotypic genus, California.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "75834501-a2a8-58ee-9d32-f22191816f1a",
        "text": "Page: Erodium. Sentence: Erodium is a genus of flowering plants in the botanical family Geraniaceae.\nPage: Erodium. Sentence: The genus includes about 60 species, native to North Africa, Indomalaya, The Middle East, and Australia.\nPage: Cymbidium. Sentence: Cymbidium , or boat orchid, is a genus of 52 evergreen species in the orchid family Orchidaceae.\nPage: California macrophylla. Sentence: It was formerly placed in the genus \"Erodium\", but was later placed in a monotypic genus of its own named California.\nPage: Cymbidium suave. Sentence: Cymbidium suave (R. Brown 1810), or the snake orchid, is an Australian orchid species that is part of the genus \"Cymbidium\" which consists of 52 species.",
